# Project Architecture

## Workspace Map

- `aiengineerapp/` is the production Next.js app. It uses pnpm, React 19, Next 16 App Router, Tailwind 4, Supabase SSR, Radix/shadcn-style UI, TipTap, nuqs, TanStack Query, Vercel AI SDK, Zod, and Vitest.
- Root `supabase/` is the Supabase CLI project. App `package.json` scripts named `db:*` use `--workdir ..` so they target the root Supabase folder.
- Root `alignment/` contains planning outputs and agent handoff docs. These are proposed architecture/planning docs, not shipped app code.
- `aiwiki/` is the vault/content source used by ingestion scripts for course/module/challenge content and other corpus assets.

## Imports And Conventions

- `tsconfig.json` maps `@/*` to the app root. Prefer `@/components/...`, `@/lib/...`, `@/types/...`, and `@/app/...`.
- Keep route `page.tsx` files thin: fetch in Server Components or call server actions, then compose from `components/`.
- Put broadly reusable UI in `components/`; route-private heavy client UI may live beside its route as `_*-shell.tsx`.
- Generated files are not hand-edited. In particular, never manually edit `types/database.types.ts`.

## App Router

| Area | Role |
|------|------|
| `app/layout.tsx` | Global fonts, `ThemeProvider`, `NuqsAdapter`, `Toaster`, metadata. |
| `app/globals.css` | Tailwind v4 import, OKLCH design tokens, app theme variables. |
| `app/(app)/` | Authenticated product shell: left rail, top bar, cmd-K, product pages. |
| `app/(auth)/` | Login, auth callback route handler, logout. |
| `app/(onboarding)/` | `/onboarding/[step]`, step config, actions, step UI. |
| `app/(marketing)/` | Public `/welcome`. |
| `app/actions/` | Cross-cutting server actions: search, explore, palette, save, follow, notes, notifications, people facets, drawer bootstrap. |

Authenticated routes currently include home, `/learn`, `/courses`, `/challenges`, `/explore`, `/explore/[type]`, `/search`, `/saved`, `/follows`, `/notes`, `/notes/[id]`, `/ask`, settings, and dossiers.

Dossier routes currently include `/p/[slug]`, `/o/[slug]`, `/talk/[slug]`, `/video/[id]`, `/lib/[slug]`, `/paper/[slug]`, and `/event/[slug]`.

`types/domain.ts` contains `ENTITY_HREF`, the canonical URL map for entity kinds. It includes some future surfaces that do not yet have `page.tsx`; add routes only when shipping those surfaces.

## Auth, Proxy, And Supabase

- `proxy.ts` is the Next 16 Proxy. It refreshes Supabase sessions and handles auth/onboarding UX redirects.
- Shared proxy/session logic lives in `lib/supabase/middleware.ts`.
- `lib/auth/require-user.ts` provides `getOptionalUser` and `requireUser`; server code should use these for authenticated user boundaries.
- RLS plus server-side `requireUser()` are the security boundary. Proxy redirects are user experience, not authorization.

Supabase clients:

- `lib/supabase/server.ts`: server component/action client using `@supabase/ssr`.
- `lib/supabase/browser.ts`: browser client.
- `lib/supabase/admin.ts`: service-role client, server-only.
- `lib/supabase/env.ts`: env helpers.

